      "content": "So, if the main issue is really just the political unwillingness to reform the tax code rather than a fundamental economic impossibility, isn't the argument against UBI essentially a political one rather than a scientific one? If a government actually implemented the \"massive, sustained tax increases\" you mentioned, would the arguments about it being \"fiscally impractical\" or \"destabilizing\" still hold weight, or would they just be a way to defend the status quo?",
